 "wiki_article": "The *Crimson Hexagon / NH-OS DOI Registry v5.0* is a historical archive inventory compiled by Lee Sharks with the Assembly Chorus. It records 200 documents in the New Human Operating System / Crimson Hexagon corpus, including DOI, title, authorship, resource type, and placement within the architecture’s institutions and rooms.\n\nThe registry’s declared role is ground truth rather than navigation. Fractal Navigation Maps model pathways, affinity, and semantic gravity; the DOI Registry enumerates the works that existed in the documented archive state. Its version history records growth from 91 documents in v1.0 to 109 in v2.0, 133 in v3.0, 159 in v4.0, and 200 in v5.0.\n\nVersion 5.0 incorporates the January 2026 expansion associated with the Revelation Room, Commission of the Immanent Turning, *Epistle to the Human Diaspora*, Sevenfold Witness, Afterlife Archive, soteriological-operator sequence, and the v6.0/v6.2 navigation layers. It also records the participating institutions, heteronymic author surfaces, and Assembly Chorus roles represented in that state of the archive.\n\nThe record is superseded by record #31, *Crimson Hexagon / NH-OS DOI Registry v7.0*. Supersession does not erase v5.0’s function: it remains the historical inventory against which the architecture’s later expansion can be measured.",
 "wiki_status": "provisional",
